--TEST--
A delegated call whose `lateinit` field is uninitialized, in a class that implements `LateInit`, calls `initProperty` first and then forwards — `rule:classes/late-init-initializes-on-the-first-read`, `rule:classes/delegation-by-property`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:classes/lateinit
interface Greeter {
  public function greet(string $who): string;
}

class Polite implements Greeter {
  public function greet(string $who): string { return "hello " . $who; }
}

class Outer implements Greeter by $inner, LateInit {
  public lateinit Polite $inner;
  public int $calls = 0;
  public function initProperty(string $name): void {
    $this->calls = $this->calls + 1;
    echo "init ", $name, "\n";
    $this->inner = new Polite();
  }
}

// An empty `initProperty` leaves the field unset, so the forward throws and
// releases its argument.
class Lazy implements Greeter by $inner, LateInit {
  public lateinit Polite $inner;
  public function initProperty(string $name): void {}
}

Outer $o = new Outer();
echo $o->greet("a" . "b"), "\n";
Greeter $g = $o;
echo $g->greet("c"), "\n";
echo "calls=", $o->calls as string, "\n";

try {
  echo (new Lazy())->greet("d" . "e"), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
  echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
init inner
hello ab
hello c
calls=1
`initProperty` returned, but `$inner` is still not initialized.
